# Tests for the account lots: NONE tag, which opts an account (and its
# subaccounts) out of lot tracking - eg for tax-sheltered accounts where
# cost basis is irrelevant. Precedence is by specificity: a posting's
# explicit cost basis annotation beats the account opt-out, which beats
# the commodity's lots: tag.

# ** 1. An account with a lots: NONE tag is not lot-tracked: no lot
# subaccounts, no gain postings, no lot errors; other accounts are
# tracked as usual.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:
account assets:ira  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy in taxable account
    assets:broker    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 buy in IRA: not lot-tracked
    assets:ira       10 AAPL @ $60
    assets:checking

2026-03-01 sell in IRA: no lots consumed, no gain calculated
    assets:ira       -5 AAPL @ $80
    assets:checking   $400
$ hledger -f- bal --lots
              5 AAPL  assets:ira
             10 AAPL  assets:broker:{2026-01-15, $50}
               $-700  assets:checking
--------------------
               $-700
             15 AAPL  

# ** 2. Moving units in kind from a tracked account into an opted-out
# account is a disposal (the units leave lot tracking), priceless here so
# no gain is calculated; add a transacted price to realise a gain.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:
account assets:ira  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy in taxable account
    assets:broker    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 move in kind to the IRA
    assets:broker   -10 AAPL
    assets:ira       10 AAPL
$ hledger -f- print --lots -x --verbose-tags date:2026-02
2026-02-01 move in kind to the IRA
    assets:broker:{2026-01-15, $50}              -10 AAPL {2026-01-15, $50}  ; ptype: dispose
    assets:ira                                    10 AAPL

>=

# ** 3. Moving units in kind from an opted-out account into a tracked
# account requires a cost basis or price on the receiving posting (a lot
# must be created).
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:
account assets:ira  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy in IRA
    assets:ira       10 AAPL @ $50
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 move in kind out of the IRA
    assets:ira      -10 AAPL
    assets:broker    10 AAPL
$ hledger -f- bal --lots
>2 /AAPL is declared lotful \(commodity lots: tag\) but this posting was not classified/
>=1

# ** 4. A posting with an explicit cost basis annotation is lot-tracked
# even in an opted-out account (the more specific declaration wins), and
# subaccounts inherit the opt-out.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:
account assets:ira  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 explicit cost basis in the IRA is still tracked
    assets:ira       10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 buy in an IRA subaccount: inherits the opt-out
    assets:ira:cash   -$600
    assets:ira:stocks  10 AAPL @ $60
$ hledger -f- bal --lots -N
               $-600  assets:ira:cash
             10 AAPL  assets:ira:stocks
             10 AAPL  assets:ira:{2026-01-15, $50}
               $-500  assets:checking

# ** 5. A subaccount can re-enable lot tracking with its own lots: method
# tag (the nearest declaration wins). The tag value is case insensitive.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:
account assets:ira  ; lots: none
account assets:ira:active  ; lots: LIFO

2026-01-15 buy in re-enabled subaccount
    assets:ira:active    10 AAPL @ $50
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 buy in opted-out parent
    assets:ira           10 AAPL @ $55
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- bal --lots -N
             10 AAPL  assets:ira
             10 AAPL  assets:ira:active:{2026-01-15, $50}
              $-1050  assets:checking

# ** 6. lots: NONE is not allowed on commodity declarations (commodities
# are untracked by default; NONE is a per-account opt-out).
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:broker    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- bal
>2 /lots: NONE is not supported on commodity declarations/
>=1

# ** 7. An opted-out account holding a commodity with a global (*ALL)
# method does not trigger the method coherence check.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots: FIFOALL
account assets:ira  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy tracked
    assets:broker    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 buy in IRA
    assets:ira       10 AAPL @ $60
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- bal --lots -N
             10 AAPL  assets:ira
             10 AAPL  assets:broker:{2026-01-15, $50}
              $-1100  assets:checking

# ** 8. An unpriced disposal with an explicit lot selector, balanced by an
# elided opted-out account posting, stays a disposal (the opt-out excludes
# the elided posting from being read as a transfer destination), and errors
# for lack of a selling price.
<
account assets:vault  ; lots: NONE

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 move out of tracking
    assets:stocks    -5 AAPL {$50}
    assets:vault

$ hledger -f- bal --lots
>2 /dispose posting has no transacted price/
>=1
